id:                     E2174-draft-2301
trigger_tool:           make|conan|cmake
phase:                  build|package|test_package
error_signature:        Library .* not found in package|conan_package_library_targets|check target
severity:               2
category:               build-system|artifact-packaging|testing|conan
match_keywords:         hand-written Makefile, check target, all target, static library, package artifact, CMakeDeps, missing library
title:                  A test target does not guarantee that the library artifact is packaged
root_cause:             A hand-written build system can define a test or check target that depends only on test executables and object files, while the archive or shared library target remains outside that dependency graph. Running check alone can therefore report passing upstream tests but leave the package without the library named by Conan package_info.libs. The consumer then fails during CMakeDeps generation with a missing-library error.
affected_scope:        Conan recipes for Makefile-based libraries and any build system where validation targets and distributable artifact targets are independent.
verification_cmd:      Build the explicit artifact target and the complete upstream test target in one bounded invocation; list the package lib/include roots before compiling an independent test_package consumer.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-artifact-and-test-targets
rec_description:        Inspect the upstream target graph before writing the recipe. Invoke the artifact target (for example all or libname.a) explicitly, then invoke check/test. After package(), assert that every library in cpp_info.libs exists under the package lib root, and run the consumer through the normal generated build files.
rec_command:            make -C <source> <artifact-target> check; test -f <package>/lib/<library>; conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<target-profile> -pr:b=<build-profile>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-build-and-consumer-test
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      artifact-only-then-test
fallback_description:   If the upstream check target is unavailable, build the named artifact first and run the smallest documented test entry separately; an artifact-only pass is not a substitute for upstream tests.
fallback_command:      make -C <source> <artifact-target>; make -C <source> check
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          explicit-target-order
forbid_1_pattern:       make .* check.*package_info.libs|check.*only.*artifact
forbid_1_reason:        A passing test executable can mask a missing distributable library and lets Conan generate a consumer configuration that cannot link.
forbid_1_consequence:   CMakeDeps or the consumer link stage fails after an apparently successful upstream test run.
forbid_2_pattern:       create.*--build=missing.*as.*package.*presence|skip.*consumer
forbid_2_reason:        A local fallback build does not prove that the package contains the declared artifact or that the published consumer contract is usable.
forbid_2_consequence:   Missing package files and target-name errors reach CI or downstream users.
principles:             P002,P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E342,E344
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
